body:
epic:#27293#1 · sunhaolin · session_017xRBcVBKAFk1ntXSjvPt7U

Filing gate: ③ a task the maintainer ordered, verbatim 「立一张维护者处理卡，让维护者在本机测试」 (2026-11-04, in this seat's session). Child of #27293 (E4). It carries the one step of #28647 that a cloud seat cannot do. ⛔ Not a claim.

Ruling-ref: 6556740185

Maintainer-action: on your own machine, run the script below with a read-only GitHub token in GITHUB_MCP_TOKEN, and post its stdout as a comment on this card — done when a comment on this card carries the script's JSON with a `toolsSnapshot` digest for both `search_issues` and `issue_read`

## 维护者速读

- 要你做什么：在自己电脑上跑下面这段脚本（Node 18 以上，不用装依赖，不用拉仓库），把它输出的 JSON 原样贴到本卡评论里。
- 为什么要你做：#28647 要给 GitHub 连接器锁定两个工具，锁定值必须对着 GitHub 的真实 MCP 服务器测出来。云端席位的网络连不上 `api.githubcopilot.com`，也没有测量用的 token，按规定不能填假值。
- token：一个只读的 GitHub 个人访问 token，能读 issue 即可（fine-grained：Issues 和 Metadata 设为 Read）。只放在本机环境变量里，⛔ 不要贴到卡上或聊天里。脚本不会打印它，输出里也没有它。
- 输出里有什么：测量时间、服务器地址、两个工具各自的 sha256，以及这两个工具的公开定义（名称、描述、参数 schema），没有任何密钥。
- 跑失败时：退出码 3 是服务器拒绝了（401 一般是 token 不对）；退出码 4 是 token 权限不够，看不到某个工具，换一个能读 issue 的 token 再跑。
- 之后：总监席核验评论后摘掉本卡的 `pm:awaiting-maintainer` 并关卡，epic 席位随即派发 #28647。开发会在容器里用仓库自带的 `computeMcpToolsSnapshot` 对你贴的工具定义重算一遍，两边一致才提交。

## The script

Save as `measure-github-mcp-pins.mjs`, then run `GITHUB_MCP_TOKEN=<token> node measure-github-mcp-pins.mjs`. Its canonical JSON and digest are the ones `packages/connectors/connector-mcp/src/tool-snapshot.ts` defines. The seat checked the script against a local mock MCP server (SSE answers, session header, a paged `tools/list`, a 401 on a wrong token), and `computeMcpToolsSnapshot` reproduced its digests exactly.

```js
// Measure the toolsSnapshot pins of packages/apps/connector-github (#28647).
// Node >= 18, no dependencies. Reads the token from GITHUB_MCP_TOKEN and never prints it.
import { createHash } from 'node:crypto';

const URL_ = process.env.MCP_URL ?? 'https://api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/';
const INCLUDE = ['search_issues', 'issue_read'];
const token = process.env.GITHUB_MCP_TOKEN;
if (!token) { console.error('GITHUB_MCP_TOKEN is not set'); process.exit(2); }

// The same canonical JSON and digest as packages/connectors/connector-mcp/src/tool-snapshot.ts.
const canonicalJson = (v) => {
  if (Array.isArray(v)) return `[${v.map((e) => (e === undefined ? 'null' : canonicalJson(e))).join(',')}]`;
  if (v !== null && typeof v === 'object') {
    return `{${Object.keys(v).filter((k) => v[k] !== undefined).sort()
      .map((k) => `${JSON.stringify(k)}:${canonicalJson(v[k])}`).join(',')}}`;
  }
  return JSON.stringify(v);
};
const digest = (t) => createHash('sha256')
  .update(canonicalJson({ name: t.name, description: t.description, inputSchema: t.inputSchema }), 'utf8')
  .digest('hex');

let sessionId; let nextId = 1;
async function rpc(method, params, notify = false) {
  const headers = {
    'content-type': 'application/json',
    accept: 'application/json, text/event-stream',
    authorization: `Bearer ${token}`,
    'x-mcp-readonly': 'true',
  };
  if (sessionId) headers['mcp-session-id'] = sessionId;
  const id = notify ? undefined : nextId++;
  const res = await fetch(URL_, { method: 'POST', headers, body: JSON.stringify({ jsonrpc: '2.0', method, params, ...(notify ? {} : { id }) }) });
  sessionId = res.headers.get('mcp-session-id') ?? sessionId;
  if (notify) return undefined;
  if (!res.ok) { console.error(`${method}: HTTP ${res.status}`); process.exit(3); }
  const text = await res.text();
  const bodies = (res.headers.get('content-type') ?? '').includes('text/event-stream')
    ? text.split(/\r?\n/).filter((l) => l.startsWith('data:')).map((l) => l.slice(5).trim()).filter(Boolean)
    : [text];
  const msg = bodies.map((b) => JSON.parse(b)).find((m) => m.id === id);
  if (!msg) { console.error(`${method}: no response with id ${id}`); process.exit(3); }
  if (msg.error) { console.error(`${method}: ${JSON.stringify(msg.error)}`); process.exit(3); }
  return msg.result;
}

await rpc('initialize', { protocolVersion: '2025-03-26', capabilities: {}, clientInfo: { name: 'objectstack-pin-measure', version: '1' } });
await rpc('notifications/initialized', undefined, true);
const tools = []; let cursor;
do { const r = await rpc('tools/list', cursor ? { cursor } : {}); tools.push(...(r.tools ?? [])); cursor = r.nextCursor; } while (cursor);

const picked = INCLUDE.map((n) => tools.find((t) => t.name === n));
const missing = INCLUDE.filter((n, i) => !picked[i]);
if (missing.length) { console.error(`not listed for this token: ${missing.join(', ')} (served ${tools.length} tools) — the token is under-scoped`); process.exit(4); }

console.log(JSON.stringify({
  measuredAt: new Date().toISOString(),
  url: URL_,
  headers: { 'X-MCP-Readonly': 'true' },
  toolsSnapshot: Object.fromEntries(picked.map((t) => [t.name, digest(t)])),
  tools: picked.map((t) => ({ name: t.name, description: t.description, inputSchema: t.inputSchema })),
}, null, 2));
```

## Business reason

#27293's Done-when gives each shelf listing a verifiable `upstream`, `commit` and `sha256`. Ruling 6556740185 (#28590 B) makes the pin set the `sha256` of an MCP app. The GitHub app is the last E4 card left, and the measurement is the only part of it that needs the live server. Since 2026-11-01 the cloud environment has neither the network route nor a measurement token (#28647 comment 6557674668). Without this step, the epic cannot close.

## Reader

- The maintainer runs the script and posts the output.
- The director seat checks the comment, then removes `pm:awaiting-maintainer` and closes this card with an evidence comment, in the same stroke.
- The epic seat then dispatches #28647 (`Blocked-by:` this card). That dev commits the posted digests, recomputes them offline with `computeMcpToolsSnapshot` over the posted `tools`, and adds the posted definitions as a test fixture. No live call is made in CI.

## Dedupe

